People ask us the same handful of questions before we start working together. Here are the answers in one place.

## Getting started

Fill out our intake form so we can learn about you and your business. If it looks like a great fit, we reach out with next steps and get a call on the calendar.

## What we need from you

Everything you have. Brand guidelines, logos, data, audience details, and one person on your team who can be our main point of contact. We work inside existing brand guidelines all the time and review them during discovery so every piece matches your look, tone, and message.

## What's included

We stretch or shrink to fit the project. Most often that means strategy, copywriting, producing, production, and post-production.

## Turnaround

It depends on the project. For social media we like to stay at least a month ahead, and we usually deliver a first round for review within the week. Custom work takes the time it needs, plus whatever time you need for review.

## Revisions and feedback

We want you to get exactly what you're after, and you're hiring us for our guidance too. So we'll always share our honest take on a change, and if you feel strongly, we make it.

## Working outside Southern California

Absolutely. We've completed more than 500 productions outside our local area. For distant locations we coordinate local crews or build travel into the budget.

## Final files

Usually a compressed version for your digital platforms and a high-quality master you can repurpose later. We confirm the exact formats for each project.

Ready to start? [Tell us about your project](/contact/).
